# AI Service Chatbot Audit Status And Plan

Last updated: 2026-04-02

## Scope

This document summarizes the current backend audit status of the Petties AI chatbot in `petties-agent-serivce/`, groups the remaining backlog by priority, and defines the next implementation batches.

Primary code areas reviewed:

- `petties-agent-serivce/app/core/agents/`
- `petties-agent-serivce/app/api/websocket/chat.py`
- `petties-agent-serivce/app/api/routes/chat.py`
- `petties-agent-serivce/app/core/database/mongodb.py`
- `petties-agent-serivce/app/core/tools/`
- `petties-agent-serivce/app/core/presentation/`
- `petties-agent-serivce/app/api/schemas/websocket_schemas.py`
- `petties-agent-serivce/tests/`

Reference documents:

- `docs-references/development/AI_SERVICE_CHATBOT_CHECKLIST.md`
- `docs-references/documentation/AI_SERVICE_AUDIT_CHECKLIST.md`

## Status Legend

- `PASS` = implemented and reasonably covered by current code/tests
- `PARTIAL` = implemented partially, or implemented without enough rigor / test coverage
- `FAIL` = not implemented yet or currently below minimum audit expectation

## Overall Assessment

- Estimated completion: `94%`
- Current quality level: `usable and fairly stable for main flows, with clearer runtime truth for booking/search behavior, safer transport path, and stronger regression coverage, but still not fully hardened for production-grade audit readiness`
- Strongest areas: booking session state, WebSocket hydration, prompt enrichment, clinic/slot routing guidance, idle-expiration reset, transport validation, focused regression tests
- Weakest areas: duplicated save-path semantics between REST and WebSocket, error-code coverage, observability, and broader conversation-policy hardening

